{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477956-what-discipline-would-manipulate-fear","id":1477956,"title":"What Discipline Would Manipulate Fear","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-03T10:30:54-07:00","id":1477956,"title":"What Discipline Would Manipulate Fear","content":"Out of all the current V20 disciplines, which one would be closest to a discipline that can manipulate fear in others? I'm converting Requiem ideas over into V20, and I can't find a good replacement for Nightmare, the Nosferatu's signature discipline. Any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-03T11:32:43-07:00","id":1477958,"title":"","content":"As for just causing fear, I think that Presence would cover that. Presence already can cause fear with Dread Gaze or Majesty. For something more complex, like making illusions of someone\u2019s worst fears, I think it would require another Discipline, such as Obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-03T12:00:33-07:00","id":1477962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477956-what-discipline-would-manipulate-fear?p=1477958#post1477958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for just causing fear, I think that Presence would cover that. Presence already can cause fear with Dread Gaze or Majesty. For something more complex, like making illusions of someone\u2019s worst fears, I think it would require another Discipline, such as Obfuscate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, Presence is not a good option, another clan calls it their signature discipline, and Obfuscate can not do such things in V20.<br /> <br /> The goal is to invoke terror into through all powers in some way or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":26764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","user":"Vilenecromancer","date":". 04-03-2022, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-03T12:24:33-07:00","id":1477964,"title":"","content":"My first thought was also Presence. If you don't want to use that, it might be better to just take convert Nightmare directly from VtR to VtM. I suspect that the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vampire_Translation_Guide\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire Translation Guide</a> might be helpful there. Alternatively, it might make sense as a Path for Blood Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-03T12:52:53-07:00","id":1477966,"title":"","content":"Without Presence, Chimerstry or Dementation, although neither are predominantly fear themed. Eye of Chaos would mess it up by making your Nosferatu seers. Maybe you could mix them up: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Dementation: Passion, except they get scared, regardless of their current emotion.</li> <li>Dementation: The Haunting.</li> <li>Chimerstry: Apparition or even Permenancy, provided it's horrific.</li> <li>Dementation: Voice of Madness or Fire Voice.</li> <li>Chimerstry: Horrid Reality.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-03T13:26:19-07:00","id":1477968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477956-what-discipline-would-manipulate-fear#post1477956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of all the current V20 disciplines, which one would be closest to a discipline that can manipulate fear in others? I'm converting Requiem ideas over into V20, and I can't find a good replacement for Nightmare, the Nosferatu's signature discipline. Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;When in doubt, Thaumaturgy on out.&quot;<br /> <br /> Check out &quot;Prey on the Soul's Fear&quot; in Dark Ages Companion (I believe Second Edition) for some ideas. <br /> <br /> Failing that, you could just keep the same Nightmare splat, rework the Disciplines a bit to make it at home in the Proper World of Darkness, and call it Gucci.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-03T14:08:03-07:00","id":1477969,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll go with Kharnov then. If you want Nightmare, then just use Nightmare and convert the rules as needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-03T14:29:40-07:00","id":1477970,"title":"","content":"Presence is the Discipline that affects emotions, and already has a power that creates fear - Dread Gaze. That's just the best fit in my opinion.<br /> <br /> But since you said you don't want that, you should go to more unusual ways to replicate it. And the prior posters have already covered the ways I'd consider doing it. Converting the Requiem power into its own Discipline or Path of Thaumaturgy. Or if there's a specific power you want to port over, maybe some kind of Combination Discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-04T00:57:01-07:00","id":1477995,"title":"","content":"There's an old DT path pertaining to fear: Path of Phobos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T10:45:41-07:00","id":1478071,"title":"","content":"Daimonions lvl 1 and 2 (Sense the Sin and Fear of the Void Below) could be worth a look as well. But yeah, Prey on the Souls Fear and Path of Phobos are good paths to look to for inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T11:00:04-07:00","id":1478074,"title":"","content":"Just pick Nightmare from requiem, the translation guide may help you with that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"